speechtext:
I believe, Mr. Speaker, if you check the records or your memory, you will realize that the government Whip got up on questions and comments. Therefore, he cannot move that particular motion. It should also be noted that he has taken almost all the time for questions and comments and, therefore, not allowing other members to speak.
I am sure, with regard to this specific point of order, because he asked a number of questions which we obviously do not have a chance to reply to since he has taken up most of the time, the motion he put is out of order.
[Translation}
